<section class="how">
    <h2>How to Use This Paint Calculator</h2>
    <p>Estimating paint volume accurately prevents extra trips to the store while avoiding wasted paint cans. Use this tool with simple step-by-step room inputs:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Room Dimensions:</strong> Enter length, width, and wall height in feet or meters.</li>
        <li><strong>Doors & Windows:</strong> Enter counts for standard doors (21 sq ft / 2 m² subtracted) and windows (15 sq ft / 1.4 m² subtracted).</li>
        <li><strong>Number of Coats:</strong> Standard interior walls require two full coats for uniform coverage and rich color depth.</li>
        <li><strong>Include Ceiling:</strong> Check the box if you plan to paint the ceiling using the same paint formula.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="formula">
    <h2>Paint Calculation Formulas & Standards</h2>
    <p>Standard architectural paint coverage calculations rely on industry benchmarks for surface area and liquid volume:</p>
    
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #2563eb;">Wall Surface Area Formula</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Total perimeter multiplied by height minus door and window openings:</p>
            <p><code>Wall Area = 2 x (Length + Width) x Height - Openings</code></p>
        </div>

        <div style="background: var(--input-bg); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; color: #7c3aed;">Gallon & Liter Spreading Rate</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 0.9rem;">Standard paint spreads at approximately 350 sq ft per gallon (9 sq meters per liter):</p>
            <p><code>Gallons = (Total Area x Coats) / 350</code></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

